reativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}, "desc_sha256": "eb91391ded17b6aa5b17c3937bcf2b880cccdc963a34fd9abf66dda7d74eb6b4"}}'' restored on Cave of Zeus, Naxos', 'eb91391ded17b6aa5b17c3937bcf2b880cccdc963a34fd9abf66dda7d74eb6b4', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On Mount Zas on Naxos, 630m above sea level, the Cave of Zeus holds large stalactites and stalagmites. In one telling, the young Zeus hid here from his father, Cronus."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the cave is on Mount Zas [S1]; it is on Naxos [S1]; it lies 630 m above sea level [S5]; large stalactites and stalagmites are inside the cave [S6]; in one telling, the young Zeus hid in the cave from his father Cronus [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-009 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Cave of Zeus is a cave (an ancient Greek cave, occupied from the Late Neolithic to Early Cycladic III) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_of_Zas_(Naxos)]; The cave is on Mount Zas on the island of Naxos (Greece) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Zas]; The cave lies 630 m above sea level [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_of_Zas_(Naxos)]; The cave holds large stalactites and stalagmites [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_of_Zas_(Naxos)]; In one telling (Agathosthenes''), Zeus spent his childhood in this cave [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_of_Zas_(Naxos)]; In that telling the young Zeus was hiding here from his father, Cronus [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_of_Zas_(Naxos)]"}]'::jsonb),
