: "Above the Bridgewater Lakes, the Tarragal Caves were identified as important Aboriginal camping places. Excavation revealed shell middens and earth ovens over 11,000 years old."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Tarragal Caves are above (overlook) the Bridgewater Lakes [S1]; the caves were identified as important Aboriginal camping places [S2]; excavation revealed shell middens [S2]; excavation revealed earth ovens [S2]; the shell middens and earth ovens are over 11,000 years old [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-010 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Tarragal Caves are a cave site (a network of limestone caves and rockshelters) above/overlooking the Bridgewater Lakes [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragal_Caves]; The caves are near Tarragal and Cape Bridgewater, Victoria (Australia) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragal_Caves]; The caves were identified as important Aboriginal camping places [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragal_Caves]; Excavation revealed shell middens over 11,000 years old [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragal_Caves]; Excavation revealed earth ovens over 11,000 years old [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragal_Caves]; The caves were excavated (by Harry Lourandos, late 1970s) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragal_Caves]"}]'::jsonb),
